# Core guardrails

- Inspect before editing; make the smallest coherent change.
- Do not invent requirements, data, setup, or test results.
- Ask when an undefined decision affects scoring, security, or stored data.
- No unrelated features, services, abstractions, dependencies, or refactors.
- No remote migrations, deployments, production-data changes, or domain changes without explicit approval.
- Enforce rules in server/database code, not UI-only checks.
- Keep scoring centralized and deterministic when implemented.
- Prefer mobile-first, accessible UI.
- Before finishing: lint, clean typecheck after `npm ci`, focused tests that exist, production build.
- Handoff must list checks actually run and migrations created vs applied.
